    "paragraphs": [
      "Mixture of experts models route each token to a small set of feed forward networks. During prompt processing, different tokens can select different experts. A useful inference engine must preserve token order for attention and recurrent state, while reusing weights across microbatches.",
      "Consider a workstation with limited GPU memory and enough CPU memory for all model weights. Explain the difference between transferring every expert in a layer and transferring only missing experts selected by the router. Discuss cache eviction, transfer latency, memory bandwidth, and the impact of batch size. Distinguish lower memory consumption from higher throughput. Describe how to measure correctness and performance without confusing model loading time with prompt evaluation time."
    ]
